# Testing

## .NET

- Domain and Application get unit tests first.
- API gets integration tests for critical endpoints.
- Prefer behavior assertions over implementation details.
- Use the solution's chosen test framework consistently (default toward MSTest skills already installed unless the solution already uses another).
- After bug fixes, add a regression test when practical.

## Angular

- Test non-trivial services and components with Vitest/`ng test`.
- Prefer testing user-visible behavior and public APIs.
- Mock HTTP at the boundary; do not hit the real API in unit tests.

## Commands

- Backend: `dotnet test`
- Frontend: `ng test` / project test script; also `ng build` after structural changes
